    "note": "**M2.4-fix — the cursor renders now.** You were right that 012 was broken: the orange box showed in **preview** but not in the **ffmpeg render**. I traced it end-to-end:\n\n- ffmpeg's `drawbox` writes the box's **RGB but not its alpha** — on the transparent canvas base (`color=black@0`) the outline kept alpha 0, so it composited to nothing. (Preview uses a non-ffmpeg path → it showed there. Classic preview/render divergence.)\n- Isolated it with a minimal 2-source repro: drawbox on an **opaque** base → visible; on a **transparent** base → gone.\n- Fix: `drawbox=…:color=…@1:replace=1` — `replace=1` overwrites the box pixels (colour **and** alpha) opaque.\n\nVerified by rendering the canvas through the real engine and sampling pixels: the orange cursor outline is present and frames the active region. Everything else (depth-1 `lavfi`, leads the parse, resizes on split/comma/close) is unchanged.\n\n_(`.mosaic` twin frozen beside this candidate.)_",
